By the Triangle Inequality, $PA \le AB + PB,$ so
\[f(x) = PA - PB \le AB = \sqrt{26}.\]Equality occurs when $x = -10$ (which makes $P,$ $B,$ and $A$ collinear).

We can write
\begin{align*}
f(x) &= \sqrt{x^2 - 10x + 34} - \sqrt{x^2 + 4} \\
&= \frac{(\sqrt{x^2 - 10x + 34} - \sqrt{x^2 + 4})(\sqrt{x^2 - 10x + 34} + \sqrt{x^2 + 4})}{\sqrt{x^2 - 10x + 34} + \sqrt{x^2 + 4}} \\
&= \frac{(x^2 - 10x + 34) - (x^2 + 4)}{\sqrt{x^2 - 10x + 34} + \sqrt{x^2 + 4}} \\
&= \frac{-10x + 30}{\sqrt{x^2 - 10x + 34} + \sqrt{x^2 + 4}}.
\end{align*}If $x \le 3,$ then $f(x) \ge 0,$ so assume $x > 3,$ so
\[f(x) = -10 \cdot \frac{x - 3}{\sqrt{x^2 - 10x + 34} + \sqrt{x^2 + 4}}.\]If $3 < x \le 7,$ then
\[\frac{x - 3}{\sqrt{x^2 - 10x + 34} + \sqrt{x^2 + 4}} = \frac{x - 3}{\sqrt{(x - 7)^2 + 9} + \sqrt{x^2 + 4}} \le \frac{2}{3 + 4} = \frac{2}{7} < \frac{1}{2},\]so $f(x) > -7.$

If $x > 7,$ then
\begin{align*}
\frac{x - 3}{\sqrt{x^2 - 10x + 34} + \sqrt{x^2 + 4}} &= \frac{x - 3}{\sqrt{(x - 7)^2 + 9} + \sqrt{x^2 + 4}} \\
&< \frac{x - 3}{x - 7 + x} \\
&= \frac{x - 3}{2x - 7} \\
&< \frac{x - 3}{2x - 6} = \frac{1}{2},
\end{align*}so $f(x) > -7.$

Furthermore, as $x$ becomes very large,
\[\frac{x - 3}{\sqrt{x^2 - 10x + 34} + \sqrt{x^2 + 4}} = \frac{1 - \frac{3}{x}}{\sqrt{1 - \frac{10}{x} + \frac{34}{x^2}} + \sqrt{1 + \frac{4}{x^2}}}\]approaches $\frac{1}{1 + 1} = \frac{1}{2},$ so $f(x)$ approaches $-7.$

Therefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $\boxed{(-7,\sqrt{26}]}.$

